Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:49:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/76] flashnext cuda: TF_FLASHNEXT_HIDDEN_SUM over
 TF_FLASHNEXT_PEER_SLOTS' mapped buffer for passes of up to 128 rows

With both on, a decode round or verify window writes its owner chain's hidden rows into the peer's buffer and adds the
peer's (fn_peer_rows_send, fn_peer_rows_add): the all-reduce's two-term sum without an NCCL launch, 10 KiB a row a
layer instead of PEER_SLOTS' owned slots. Longer passes keep the hidden all-reduce. TF_FLASHNEXT_OWNER_SLOTS yields to
PEER_SLOTS for the passes the mapped buffer takes.
